{
  "configuration_id": "config_034",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) achieves 0.5305 acc (config_002), far exceeding image-only (resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.3275 (config_042). Multiprofile+avgpool consistently helps both modalities. The critical open question is whether combining the dominant RNA signal with the weaker image signal via fusion actually improves over the RNA-only baseline, or whether image adds noise. Config_034 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the minimal single-variable extension of config_002: it keeps the exact same RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation, and only adds the image modality with a weighted fusion. This isolates the effect of multimodal fusion on the best-performing RNA configuration. If it beats 0.53, we confirm image contributes complementary information and can explore better fusion/encoders; if it matches or falls below, we learn image adds little value with resnet50 and should prioritize RNA-side improvements. This is the highest-information experiment under budget constraints because it directly tests the central design question (does multimodal help?) with a clean comparison to an already-established baseline."
}

